{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added per-feed `fetch_timeout` (integer seconds, 0 = use global timeout).\n\n- Migration: new `feeds.fetch_timeout int not null default 0` column.\n- Model: `Feed.FetchTimeout` (`fetch_timeout` in the API feed object), `FeedModificationRequest.FetchTimeout` patched on `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}`, and `Feed.HTTPClientTimeout()` which returns the per-feed value when > 0, otherwise the global one.\n- Storage: column is read in the feed query builder and written in `UpdateFeed`.\n- Fetching: feed refresh, entry processing/scraping and icon fetching now use `feed.HTTPClientTimeout()` instead of the global timeout.\n- Validator: rejects values below 0 or above 86400 on modification.\n- Go client: `fetch_timeout` added to `Feed` and `FeedModificationRequest`.\n\nExisting checks pass (53 unit packages, 102 integration tests); the new behaviour itself is not covered by any test I ran.\n\nNot done:\n- `fetch_timeout` is not accepted on feed creation (`POST /v1/feeds`), only on update.\n- There is no field for it in the web UI edit form.\n- The validation error is a plain English string, not a translated locale key.\n- The 86400-second upper bound is my own choice, not from the task.", "t": 1794464008.928}
